# React component guidance

## Current component patterns

- Components are written as named function exports
- Shared UI primitives live in `gtp-telemetry/src/components/shared/`
- Most dashboard panels accept `analysis: SessionAnalysis`
- `SessionHeader` is an intentional exception: it reads state from the store and handles reload/export actions

## Preferred dashboard conventions

- Keep calculation-heavy logic in `analysis-engine.ts` when possible instead of re-deriving data in the UI
- Use `Card` for panel framing and `MetricRow` / `StatusBadge` for compact metric display
- Reuse colors and thresholds from `gtp-telemetry/src/lib/constants.ts` rather than hardcoding new ones in components
- Guard optional analysis fields and channels; some parsed sessions degrade gracefully instead of providing every metric

## Import and structure expectations

- Use the existing relative import style already present in the app
- Preserve lazy-loaded panel boundaries defined in `gtp-telemetry/src/App.tsx`
- Keep shared components generic; telemetry-specific reasoning belongs in lib or dashboard-specific files
